  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22xdtz4kk2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "People who have no contact with coders seem to have no idea how much an entire profession transformed in less than a year due to AI. It is so weird to still see comments here that AI hasn’t changed anything or that AI code is bad or that companies are retreating from AI use. Does not match reality.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n22xdtz4kk2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T22:00:44.261Z",
      "likes": 508,
      "replies": 29,
      "reposts": 66,
      "score": 8.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.8,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 21.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzzzl3lbbs2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "In a little over a week we will see the release of The Last Human Game.\n\nThere will never be another AAA game at the scale of GTA 6 with no AI assistance. People in the future will look back at an all-human game with an billion dollar budget and wonder how they did it, like the Pyramids.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzzzl3lbbs2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T13:07:54.824Z",
      "likes": 175,
      "replies": 20,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 7.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 30.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n22xsngwis2i",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This is not an argument that AI is all good or a hype post that you should learn AI today or fall behind. I think there is a limited time to engage with this transition and decide how to use AI in ways that make professions work better and center humans. Ignoring reality will not get us there.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n22xsngwis2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-11T22:09:00.695Z",
      "likes": 150,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 21.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n24rilt2uc2y",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Why is this a big blow to AI boom? NVIDIA will continue to make chip and sell them. People will continue to use those chips. Maybe fewer go to Chinese black markets? Maybe it increases availability in the domestic market. But probably nothing changes except less showmanship involving leather jackets",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n24rilt2uc2y",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-12T15:21:20.474Z",
      "likes": 42,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 5,
      "score": 6.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 4.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n24xvcnir22i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "oh I see why some people are predicting financial doom regarding Jensen's departure from NVIDIA. The new CEO, Colette Kress, was the CFO and has been opposed to circular financing deals. No more questionable free rides for datacenters and hyperscalers (that will make the AI grifters sad).",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n24xvcnir22i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-12T17:15:49.517Z",
      "likes": 18,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 5.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:cnu74q3fooq4q2ty5knusr72/app.bsky.feed.post/3n24qvexgqk2k",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "How are LLMs changing scientific peer review, and what happens when conferences implement different LLM-use policies for reviewers?\n\nIn our new paper, we investigate these questions through a large-scale RCT and an anonymous survey at #ICML2026.\n\n1/5",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n24qvexgqk2k",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-12T15:10:35.743Z",
      "likes": 15,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 5.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 4.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzltzpjm3k2c",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I’m still kind of baffled by how surprised or even disbelieving some university admin are when I tell them that many (most? need more data) students are not all in on AI, actually…",
